# Eval harness. The query set is source and is committed. Everything the
# harness derives from other people's pages stays local.
#
# The labels are local on purpose, not just for size. Grading a corpus honestly
# means recording which pages are content farms, which are AI filler, and which
# are simply wrong — by name. That is sound research method and a bad thing to
# publish: it is a permanent, machine-readable, publicly attributed judgement on
# named third-party sites, and this repository is here to distribute the search
# machinery, not that. The corpus is local too, so committed labels would not
# let anyone reproduce a run anyway.
eval/corpus/
eval/corpus-*/
eval/runs/
eval/labels/

# Local experiment artifacts: scratch build output, cached scores, downloaded
# model weights. All re-derivable, none of it belongs in the repository.
dist-exp/
eval/experiments/
.model-cache/